{"id":"b7eb0840-16c0-45ef-9482-8821ecfd415b","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The parameter 'args' is an array reference provided for the main method and is never null when run from the command line.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298325Z"}
{"id":"83b40064-ea7e-4b25-a6c3-925ccd4f6d99","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is 0, we don't perform the division; otherwise, the result is a divided by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298988Z"}
{"id":"eac74039-8921-40c2-9c1e-efb9c1ea1a51","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The array of arguments is typically expected to be non-null when invoking main, as per Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298391Z"}
{"id":"f82d0519-187c-4293-99cf-ce26454c03d2","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE as a designated 'error' value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298988Z"}
{"id":"f9e2cbf2-bd7e-4b03-bb47-5144b4d4e2f0","expr":"b == 0 || b * (a / b) <= a && b * (a / b) >= (a - Math.abs(b) + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, b * (a / b) provides the largest multiple of b less than or equal to a (for positive b), capturing properties of integer division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.299821Z"}
{"id":"f326bbc5-23c1-431f-b1bf-4b3c1657043a","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"An array's length is always non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298325Z"}
{"id":"0622f2cc-1b25-4278-8326-545bf69c6b88","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + a % b == a","rationale":"For b != 0, the division and remainder relationship holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.299821Z"}
{"id":"621fff2c-1584-4138-ae69-17b2e8c61f22","expr":"b == 0 || result * b == a - (a % b)","rationale":"If b is not 0, result equals a / b; thus, result * b is a - remainder.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298988Z"}
{"id":"084220f2-2f60-4161-a0c4-9350db3357fb","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length in Java is always non-negative, so this must hold for String[] args.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298391Z"}
{"id":"9c1cdd1f-3262-4a4b-b66e-6fd58722cdcf","expr":"b != 0 || result < 0","rationale":"When b is 0, the result is Integer.MIN_VALUE, which is a negative number.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298988Z"}
{"id":"60bb7942-ca8a-4375-980e-2b1b0eaa28c6","expr":"b != Integer.MIN_VALUE || b != 0","rationale":"b can be Integer.MIN_VALUE or zero, but special care might be required in those extreme values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.299821Z"}
{"id":"c7f24886-b6c1-41f9-8c8d-646ce8c7e8be","expr":"Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"The absolute value of the quotient (when b != 0) or the special value is always less than or equal to |a|.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:45.298988Z"}
